+          "source": "lem-parameter-ode-flow-tangent-on-common-tube",
+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "Let $\\Theta\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m$ and $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d\\times\\Theta$ be open, and let $f:D\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be continuously differentiable. Let $V_\\theta\\subseteq\\Theta$ be open and $u_0:V_\\theta\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be $C^1$. Assume there is a bounded convex open set $O\\subset D$ with compact closure in $D$ such that for every $\\theta\\in V_\\theta$ the unique solution of $u'=f(t,u,\\theta)$, $u(0)=u_0(\\theta)$, exists on $[0,T]$, and all triples $(t,u_\\theta(t),\\theta)$ lie in $O$. Then $\\theta\\mapsto u_\\theta$ is $C^1$ as a map to $C([0,T];\\mathbb R^d)$. For any $\\theta_0\\in V_\\theta$, its tangent matrix $S(t)=D_\\theta u_\\theta(t)|_{\\theta=\\theta_0}$ is the unique solution of\n$$S'(t)=D_u f(t,u_{\\theta_0}(t),\\theta_0)S(t)+D_\\theta f(t,u_{\\theta_0}(t),\\theta_0),\\qquad S(0)=D u_0(\\theta_0).$$\nThe result is local to the stated common compact tube and claims no differentiability outside it.",
