+          "source_section": "Statement",
+          "quote": "Let $d,N,p\\ge1$, $T>0$, $h=T/N$, and $t_n=nh$. Let $y:[0,T]\\to\\mathbb R^d$ solve an initial-value problem in an open time-state domain $D$. Use the Euclidean norm $\\|v\\|_2=(\\sum_{i=1}^d v_i^2)^{1/2}$ of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], whose triangle inequality is proved in [[thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm]]. Let $\\mathcal T\\subset D$ be a common compact time-state tube with positive margin in $D$, and write $\\mathcal T_t:=\\{v\\in\\mathbb R^d:(t,v)\\in\\mathcal T\\}$. Suppose a one-step map $\\Psi_{h,n}$ is defined on $\\mathcal T_{t_n}$, produces $y_{n+1}=\\Psi_{h,n}(y_n)$, and the entire exact path, all numerical grid states, and every method stage lie in $\\mathcal T$. If constants $C,C_0,L\\ge0$, independent of $N$ and $n$, satisfy\n$$\\|y_0-y(0)\\|_2\\le C_0h^p,\\qquad \\|\\Psi_{h,n}(y(t_n))-y(t_{n+1})\\|_2\\le Ch^{p+1},$$\nand\n$$\\|\\Psi_{h,n}(u)-\\Psi_{h,n}(v)\\|_2\\le(1+Lh)\\|u-v\\|_2$$\nfor every $u,v\\in\\mathcal T_{t_n}$ and $0\\le n<N$, then, for $L>0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|y_n-y(t_n)\\|_2\\le\\left(C_0\\exp(LT)+C\\frac{\\exp(LT)-1}{L}\\right)h^p,$$\nand, for $L=0$,\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|y_n-y(t_n)\\|_2\\le(C_0+CT)h^p.$$",
