           "fact": "F1",
           "source": "alg-ctrl1-runge-kutta-shooting-and-collocation-transcription",
           "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "Take a mesh $0=t_0<\\cdots<t_N=T$, a pointwise-defined smooth-data model from [[def-ctrl1-smooth-transcription-data]], a control parameterization from [[def-ctrl1-control-mesh-and-piecewise-constant-parameterization]], an explicit tableau from [[def-explicit-runge-kutta-tableau-and-stage-map]], and a possibly implicit t",
+          "quote": "**Inputs.** Supply pointwise smooth data on $[0,T]$ from [[def-ctrl1-smooth-transcription-data]], an original mesh, a piecewise-constant control parameterization, an explicit tableau from [[def-explicit-runge-kutta-tableau-and-stage-map]] or a possibly implicit tableau from [[def-ctrl1-runge-kutta-tableau-and-stage-collocation]], one of `single-shooting`, `multiple-shooting`, or `collocation` mode, a finite smooth representation of the control constraints when a solver-ready NLP is requested, finite sets of declared path-constraint times, endpoint constraints, the tableau quadrature rule, an initial decision vector $z_0$ and multiplier vector $\\mu_0$, a stage residual tolerance $\\tau_s\\ge0$, a quadrature error tolerance $\\tau_q\\ge0$, a stage Newton correction cap $M_s\\in\\mathbb N_0$, and a maximum number of mesh nodes. Supply a deterministic derivative evaluator for the actual returned stage maps and resulting finite NLP on an open neighborhood of the queried candidate. On a locally fixed strict stopping branch of the finite stage-iteration procedure, differentiate that finite graph, including when the residual happens to be exactly zero at the queried point. Implicit differentiation as in [[thm-implicit-differentiation-forward-and-adjoint-formulas]] is permitted only when the selected returned stage map is certified to agree on that neighborhood with the exact local solution branch and its residual Jacobian is nonsingular there; an exact residual at the queried point alone does not establish this agreement. Return `derivative-failure` when no derivative of the actual returned map is available. Supply a quadrature error evaluator which returns a certified upper bound for the objective quadrature discrepancy or `unavailable`. Each supplied evaluator returns a value or failure in finite time. An optional trajectory-estimation request supplies the inputs of [[alg-bounded-adaptive-runge-kutta-controller]].\n$$X_{j,i}=X_{j,0}+h_j\\sum_{k<i}a_{ik}F_{j,k},\\quad t_{j,i}=t_j+c_ih_j,\\quad F_{j,i}=f(t_{j,i},X_{j,i},u_j),\\quad \\Phi_j(X_{j,0},u_j)=X_{j,0}+h_j\\sum_i b_iF_{j,i}.$$\n\n**Mesh and constraints.** Check $0=t_0<\\cdots<t_N=T$, all declared constraint and quadrature times in $[0,T]$, and all stage times $t_j+c_i h_j$ in $[0,T]$ before querying $f$ or $L$. An invalid time returns `mesh-domain-failure` with no evaluation. Insert every declared path-constraint time not already a node into the mesh, unless this exceeds the supplied node cap, in which case return `mesh-budget-exhausted`. Tie each inserted subcell's control to its original containing cell, so the parameterization is unchanged. A path constraint is evaluated at its declared times, now mesh nodes; an endpoint constraint is evaluated at its declared endpoint. This is finite sampling and does not assert continuous-path feasibility.\n\n**Stage evaluation.** On each cell write $h_j=t_{j+1}-t_j$ and $u_j$ for its tied constant control. For an explicit tableau, form the stages recursively by the displayed equations. Before each query of $f$ or $L$, check that the time is in $[0,T]$, the state lies in $\\Omega_x$, and the control lies in $\\Omega_u$; a failed membership check returns `stage-domain-failure`, and an unavailable function value returns `stage-evaluation-failure` with the cell and stage index. Apply the same checks to every declared path-constraint evaluation.\n\nFor an implicit tableau, do not leave the collocation stages as outer NLP decision variables. Form the coupled slope residual\n$$R_j(K;X_{j,0},u_j)_i=K_i-f\\!\\left(t_j+c_ih_j,X_{j,0}+h_j\\sum_k a_{ik}K_k,u_j\\right),\\quad i=1,\\ldots,s.$$\nIts open domain consists of stage vectors for which every state-control input is in the smooth-data tube. In the sampled linear-quadratic branch, form the finite matrix $M_j$ with blocks $(M_j)_{ik}=\\delta_{ik}I-h_ja_{ik}A(t_{j,i})$ and right-hand side $r_i=A(t_{j,i})X_{j,0}+B(t_{j,i})u_j$. Use exact Gaussian elimination on the stored sample coefficients: scan columns left to right, pivot on the first nonzero entry at or below the current row, swap, eliminate below, and back-substitute. If no pivot is available, return `singular-stage-matrix`; otherwise the exact solution of $M_jK=r$ is the stage vector and the nonlinear-solve status is `exact-linear-stage-solve`. In all other smooth cases, form the deterministic initial guess $K_i^{(0)}=f(t_j,X_{j,0},u_j)$ after checking that this query is defined. Before calling Newton, check that the entire seed $K^{(0)}$ belongs to the declared open domain of $R_j$, equivalently that every induced stage state lies in $\\Omega_x$ and every required control lies in $\\Omega_u$. If this check fails, return `stage-domain-failure` with the failing cell and stage index, the partial result record, and no objective candidate. Otherwise call [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]] on $R_j$ with that open evaluation domain, tolerance $\\tau_s$ and cap $M_s$. Record its iterate, residual vector, and exact status for each cell. Only `root` supplies a stage candidate; it means $\\|R_j\\|_2\\le\\tau_s$, not an exact root unless $\\tau_s=0$. Any other status returns the partial result record with `nlp_status=stage-solve-failure`, the failing cell, and no objective candidate. On a returned stage vector use $X_{j,i}=X_{j,0}+h_j\\sum_k a_{ik}K_k$ and $\\Phi_j=X_{j,0}+h_j\\sum_i b_iK_i$. A singular stage Jacobian or failed stage query is reported, not interpreted as lack of an exact solution.\n\n**Transcription modes.** In single shooting, the decision variables are the original-cell controls; set $X_{0,0}=x_0$ and recursively compute $X_{j+1,0}=\\Phi_j(X_{j,0},u_j)$. In multiple shooting, the decision variables are node states and controls; fix $X_{0,0}=x_0$ and define defects $d_j=X_{j+1,0}-\\Phi_j(X_{j,0},u_j)$. In collocation mode, use the same node/control variables and solved internal stage states; the collocation equations are solved internally by the implicit-stage procedure above. Explicit stages are likewise internal deterministic evaluations. In every mode the finite feasible set includes $u_j\\in U_c$ for each original cell. The finite objective is $\\sum_j h_j\\sum_i b_iL(t_{j,i},X_{j,i},u_j)+\\phi(X_{N,0})$, and the finite constraints are exactly the declared node/time constraints, the represented control constraints, and endpoint constraints. If $U_c$ is available only as a compact set-membership constraint and has no finite smooth representation, return the finite set-constrained model with `nlp_status=not-smooth-nlp`; the dispatcher must not treat it as an SQP-ready NLP. A QP solver route additionally requires the sampled control constraints to be affine.\n\n**Output.** Evaluate the supplied initial candidate and return a record containing its ordered decision variables, defect residuals, per-cell implicit-stage residuals, path/endpoint constraint residuals, KKT residuals, and objective value, when available. For equality residual $h$, inequality residual $g\\le0$, and multiplier pair $(\\nu,\\lambda)$, report $r_p=(h,[g]_+)$, $r_d=\\nabla J_N+Dh^T\\nu+Dg^T\\lambda$, $r_\\lambda=[-\\lambda]_+$, and $r_c=\\lambda\\odot g$. Include a model that can reevaluate these quantities at a later solver candidate. Return separate `nlp_status`, per-cell `implicit_stage_status`, optional `ivp_status`, `quadrature_status`, `mesh_status`, and `budget_status` fields. A quadrature bound at most $\\tau_q$ is `bound-met`; a larger bound is `bound-not-met`; an unavailable bound is `unavailable`. The build-stage budget field is `not-run`; the solver dispatcher fills its final value. A failed derivative evaluation leaves KKT residuals unavailable with its exact status. An unevaluated optional IVP estimate is `not-requested`; if requested, report the adaptive controller's exact finite status, not an error certificate.\n\nThis direct transcription samples pointwise data; an $L^\\infty$ equivalence class without a chosen representative and 