+          "quote": "For the data of [[def-ctrl1-linear-lqr-control-problem]] and an admissible control $u$ with state $x_u$, a **continuous LQR adjoint** is an absolutely continuous curve $p:[0,T]\\to\\mathbb R^n$ satisfying, almost everywhere,\n$$\n-\\dot p(t)=A(t)^Tp(t)+Q(t)(x_u(t)-x_d(t)),\\qquad p(T)=P(x_u(T)-x_T).\n$$\nThe equation defines the adjoint notion without asserting existence. Existence and uniqueness for each admissible control are established under Countable Choice by [[lem-ctrl1-lqr-adjoint-exists-uniquely]]. This sign convention is the one for the minimization Hamiltonian $H(t,x,p,u)=L(t,x,u)+p^T(A(t)x+B(t)u)$.",
